.venv/
.env
# ...except the one inside a test fixture, which is there to be analysed rather than read:
# the analyser looks for `.env` by that exact name, so the fixture cannot call it anything
# else and still cover it.
!tests/unit/fixtures/**/.env
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
# The frontend build output. Not committed: the build backend packs this directory from
# disk rather than from git, and every target that serves or ships it (`web`, `build`,
# `test-browser`) builds it first, so the wheel carries a fresh bundle either way. When it
# is absent the server answers `frontend_not_built` instead of failing to start.
src/archcompass/presentation/web/static/
.archcompass/
reports/
# What `evaluation/retrieval-evaluation.ipynb` builds to answer a question: the embedded
# policy index and whatever a run scored. Both are rebuilt from the dataset and the
# corpus, and the index alone is 2 MB of vectors that change with every embedding model.
evaluation/results/
# ...except an example repository's own reports package: examples/cases ships whole
# repositories to be analysed, and one of them keeps a subsystem by that name on
# purpose — it is half of the seeded PAGE_SIZE coincidence.
!examples/cases/**/reports/
frontend/node_modules/
# Vitest writes its cache next to whatever directory it was invoked from, so running the
# frontend suite from the repository root leaves a `node_modules` here holding nothing else.
node_modules/
frontend/coverage/
frontend/*.tsbuildinfo
# Local agent orientation, kept out of the repository.
.agents/
.claude/

*.log
*.impeccable/*
.DS_Store
